# G056 — Image Gallery

*v2. See `image-gallery.md` for prose: tag-set algebra (intersection, union,
difference), content-hash dedup, albums as curated subsets.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Trip Report with Content Dedup

[trip-report @week-tag @week-name @user
    IN ORDER TO
        build a travel album for the week
        excluding private images
        collapsing content duplicates so one photo appears once

    @candidates <- [gallery[with-all-tags {tags: ["travel", @week-tag]}]]
                   - [gallery[with-any-tag {tags: ["private"]}]]
    @unique     <- [gallery[dedup-by-hash {images: @candidates}]]

    @album <- [gallery[create-album
                         {id: @week-tag,
                          name: "Trip — " + @week-name,
                          curator: @user,
                          image-ids: @unique:ids}]]

    concurrent [
        <- @sarah{draft captions for: @unique}
        <- @ellie{oversight review of: @album}
    ]
    join

    @album
        where
            no image has the "private" tag
            and unique image count equals distinct content-hash count
            and curator equals @user
        || -> #album-rejected @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[gallery
    new
    add-image          {image}
    tag                {image-id, ...tags}
    untag              {image-id, ...tags}
    with-all-tags      {tags}                  ;; intersection
    with-any-tag       {tags}                  ;; union
    without-tags       {include, exclude}      ;; difference
    duplicates                                  ;; hash -> [image-id]
    find-by-hash       {content-hash}
    dedup-by-hash      {images}
    create-album       {album}
    add-to-album       {album-id, image-id}
    album-contents     {album-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: tag set algebra as resolver-registered operators

[@candidates <- @travel-tagged ∩ @week-tagged - @private-tagged
    where
        ∩ is set intersection over image ids
        and - is set difference
        and ∪ is set union (not used here but available)
]

Resolver registers set operators. Choreographies compose them
naturally. The v1 insight "set algebra is the natural query language
for tag overlaps" becomes literal syntax.

---

## Content-hash dedup as exact-equality invariant

[gallery[dedup-by-hash {images: @list}
    where
        output keeps exactly one image per distinct content-hash
        and ordering preserves first-seen precedence
        so callers get deterministic dedup
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @g <- [gallery[new]]
    [gallery[add-image {image: {id: 1, path: "/a.jpg",
                                  hash: "abc", tags: ["travel", "week-1"]}}]]
    [gallery[add-image {image: {id: 2, path: "/b.jpg",
                                  hash: "abc", tags: ["travel", "week-1"]}}]]
    [gallery[add-image {image: {id: 3, path: "/c.jpg",
                                  hash: "def", tags: ["travel", "private"]}}]]

    @travel <- [gallery[with-all-tags {tags: ["travel"]}]]
    -> @travel:count                                   ;; -> 3

    @public <- @travel - [gallery[with-any-tag {tags: ["private"]}]]
    -> @public:count                                   ;; -> 2 (images 1 and 2)

    @unique <- [gallery[dedup-by-hash {images: @public}]]
    -> @unique:count                                   ;; -> 1 (same hash "abc")

    @dupes <- [gallery[duplicates]]
    -> @dupes["abc"]                                    ;; -> [1, 2]
]
